{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"Reported as a minor aside alongside the archived-child claim bug (b7a2-4453-3bbd-4a54) by a\nrebar client installing from source.\n\n`pipx install \"<path>[agents]\"` fails with:\n\n```\npipx needs uv>=0.9.17, but ... reports 0.7.18\n```\n\n`pipx install --backend pip \"<path>[agents]\"` is a clean workaround, but the error surfaces at\ninstall time with nothing to indicate rebar itself is fine — it reads as a rebar packaging\nproblem when it is a pipx/uv version mismatch on the host.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. The install documentation (`docs/local-dev-env.md` and/or the README install section, wherever\n   the pipx path is documented) notes the pipx→uv version requirement and gives\n   `--backend pip` as the workaround, stating explicitly that this is a host toolchain issue and\n   not a rebar packaging defect.\n2. `make lint` green (docs-only change otherwise).\n"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785199727924819001,"uuid":"8d35d617-60db-4829-9ec7-8563f58d1307"}